op6: Adreno 630 bring-up in the kernel (GPU milestone G1)

New IOService SweetGPU (IOResources personality, like SweetBattery) that
starts only on /chosen/sweet-board = "oneplus,enchilada" with boot-arg
sweetgpu=1 (bring up, test, power down) or sweetgpu=2 (leave the GPU on);
sweetgpudelay=N seconds (default 30). A thread bound to cpu 0 runs
bsd/dev/sweet_gpu.c: cmd-db votes, CX GDSC + GMU clocks, GPU SMMU (GPU CB,
GMU CB, SID 0/4/5, 4K PTEs), a630_gmu.bin -> 0xBABEFACE, HFI v1, GX via
GMU OOB (710 MHz), zap via TZ PAS 13, SQE, CP_ME_INIT, SET_SECURE_MODE 0,
CP_MEM_WRITE 0xC0FFEE01, read back; every step logged "SWEET GPU: ...".
Firmware comes from the ADT node /sweet-gpu (gmu-/sqe-/zap-firmware,
dma-region) written by op6/tools/mkadt-op6.py --gpu-fw DIR; GPU-visible
memory is a carve-out outside the XNU span mapped Normal non-cacheable
(ml_io_map_unmappable + VM_WIMG_WCOMB: the 8 MiB io_submap cannot hold it).

Origin: port of the ios-op6 bare-metal shim stages op6/shim/gpu.c,
m10.c-m13.c and rpmh.c (this project, MIT; verified on the OnePlus 6
2026-11-10, op6/GPU-NOTES.md). No HackiOS, Linux or Bergamota code.
Applies on top of 0106 (xnu-8796.141.3 + 0000-0106).

