+/*
+ * SWEET GPU, milestone G1 (OnePlus 6, Adreno 630 / SDM845): the kernel
+ * brings the GPU up once, after boot, and proves the command processor runs
+ * by letting it write 0xC0FFEE01 to RAM through the GPU SMMU.
+ *
+ * This is the in-kernel port of the OP6 bare-metal shim stages that ran on
+ * the phone (op6/shim/gpu.c, m10.c, m11.c, m12.c, m13.c and the cmd-db reads
+ * of rpmh.c; ios-op6 project code, MIT; results in op6/GPU-NOTES.md "Device
+ * results", 2026-11-10). The register sequence is unchanged; what differs
+ * is only the environment:
+ *
+ *   - MMIO through ml_io_map (Device), every access a single ldr/str;
+ *   - GPU/GMU-visible memory comes from a carve-out OUTSIDE the XNU RAM
+ *     span (ADT /sweet-gpu dma-region, default 0xa0000000 + 16 MiB, free
+ *     RAM per the OP6 scan), mapped Normal non-cacheable (ml_io_map_unmappable
+ *     with VM_WIMG_WCOMB, from kernel_map: the io_submap is only 8 MiB):
+ *     the same "no cache in the way" view the shim had with the MMU off,
+ *     so no cache maintenance and no aliasing with XNU's cached physmap;
+ *   - firmware (a630_gmu.bin, a630_sqe.fw, a630_zap.mbn) from the ADT node
+ *     /sweet-gpu, put there by op6/tools/mkadt-op6.py --gpu-fw DIR (never
+ *     committed); the kernel needs no filesystem for it;
+ *   - polled (no GPU interrupt yet), from a kernel thread bound to cpu 0
+ *     (the TZ SCM INTERRUPTED/resume loop stays on one core).
+ *
+ * Sequence (each step printed before it runs, "SWEET GPU: ..."):
+ *   1 cmd-db ARC lists -> GX/CX perf votes; CX GDSC + GMU clocks 200 MHz
+ *   2 GPU SMMU: GPU on the first free context bank, GMU on the next; GMU
+ *     tables (dummy/debug/log/HFI at 0x60000000), SID 5 + 4, ATS1PR check
+ *   3 RSC/PDC micro-code, a630_gmu.bin into ITCM, GMU_RPMH_CTRL 0xf11,
+ *     CM3 released -> 0xBABEFACE
+ *   4 GX: BOOT_SLUMBER_OPTION 0, GX/MX vote of 710 MHz, OOB BOOT_SLUMBER,
+ *     SPTPRAC; HFI v1 INIT/FW_VERSION/PERF/BW/TEST; DCVS; OOB GPU_SET
+ *   5 zap via TZ (PAS 13: init_image, mem_setup, copy to 0x8c415000,
+ *     auth_and_reset; pas_is_supported answers 0 on this firmware and is
+ *     only logged)
+ *   6 SQE, GPU context (SID 0, 4K PTEs, HUPCF, USFCFG), hw_init a630
+ *     subset, ring 32K, CP_ME_INIT, CP_SET_SECURE_MODE 0, CP_NOP +
+ *     CP_MEM_WRITE 0xC0FFEE01 -> scratch read back
+ *   7 sweetgpu=1: OOB clear, VBIF halt, slumber, CM3 reset (the shim's
+ *     verified shutdown). sweetgpu=2: GPU left on (GX held by GPU_SET).
+ *
+ * Linux (GPL) and Bergamota (no licence) were facts-only sources of the
+ * shim, see op6/GPU-NOTES.md; nothing from either is copied here.
+ */
